Subject: [PATCH 10/12] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 10;
 built on 5c7abd72a with the ten patches of series 4, the move of the old
 front pages and the first nine of series 5 applied): A WORD OF MENTION
 EXCUSES A PHRASE ONLY WHERE IT STANDS WITH IT (main's M13, its second item,
 from the first file of Review 80). The sweep's own comment says a line is a
 mention if it carries a word of mention near the phrase. What was read was
 the line: one such word anywhere on it excused every phrase on it. A row of a
 table is one line, and so is a paragraph of a running log, some of them four
 thousand characters long. Main's case: a live sentence in one cell of a row
 and an unrelated word of mention in the next was not reported. THE MEND: the
 word must stand in the phrase's own cell, between the bars on either side of
 it; and on a line that is not a row of a table it must also be within 200
 characters of the phrase, before or after. A row written without its first
 bar is read both ways. A strike-through is taken off with the markup, so it
 is looked for on the line as written. WHAT WAS MEASURED FIRST, on main's
 5c7abd72a: 63 phrases stand on a line that carries such a word. 22 are in a
 row of a table, each with the word in its own cell, so the rule of the cell
 turns nothing red. Of the other 41, 39 have the word within 150 characters.
 TWO LINES OF MAIN'S TURN RED, AND THEY ARE MAIN'S TO MEND:
 docs/CAMPAIGN_STATUS.md, line 751, and docs/retired/SUBMISSION_CAMPAIGN.md,
 line 214, hold one sentence, written on 2026-09-17: that a lock passes alone
 and failed once under the load of a 146-file run. The registry withdrew that
 reading: the failing set is reproducible per seed and does not depend on
 load. The nearest word of mention is 776 characters away and is about another
 matter, so the sweep has excused the sentence since the day the phrase was
 registered. The two are not held by name in this patch: a sentence that
 states a withdrawn reading live is what the sweep is for. Until they are
 mended the gate is red on the series, and with it the one test of this lock
 that reads this repository, and main's tests that every gate passes. The
 sweep takes 3.9 seconds on this machine where it took 5.5: it looks for a
 word of mention only on a line that holds a phrase. WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH:
 an unrelated word of mention inside the phrase's own cell, or within 200
 characters of it in prose, still excuses it. The lock: two tests added to
 tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py. On the commit before, both fail:
 the sweep passes on main's row, and on a line where the only word of mention
 is more than 300 characters from the phrase. Tested against planted errors;
 reproduced, main's case; computed once. 0 of 19.

